<title>UK: Blair follows Major as century's youngest premier.</title>
<headline>Blair follows Major as century's youngest premier.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tony Blair, leader of the Labour Party, became the youngest British prime minister of the 20th century on Friday when Labour swept to a landslide victory.</p>
<p>He succeeds John Major, leader of the Conservative Party defeated in the election.</p>
<p>Chronological list of British Prime Ministers with the date</p>
<p>they first took office, and their age on taking office:</p>
<p> Arthur Balfour (Conservative)	     12 July  1902     53</p>
<p> Sir Henry Campbell-Bannerman (Liberal)   5 Dec   1905     69</p>
<p> Herbert Asquith (Liberal)		    7 April 1908     55</p>
<p> Asquith (Coalition)			   25 May   1915     --</p>
<p> David Lloyd-George (Coalition)	     7 Dec   1916     53</p>
<p> Andrew Bonar Law (Conservative)	   23 Oct   1922     63</p>
<p> Stanley Baldwin (Conservative)	    22 May   1923     56</p>
<p> Ramsay MacDonald (Labour)		   22 Jan   1924     58</p>
<p> Baldwin					    4 Nov   1924     --</p>
<p> MacDonald					  5 Jun   1929     --</p>
<p> MacDonald (Coalition)			 24 Aug   1931     --</p>
<p> Baldwin (Coalition)			    7 Jun   1935     --</p>
<p> Neville Chamberlain (Coalition)	   28 May   1937     68</p>
<p> Winston Churchill (Coalition)	     10 May   1940     65</p>
<p> Churchill (Conservative)		    23 May   1945     --</p>
<p> Clement Atlee (Labour)			26 July  1945     62</p>
<p> Churchill (Conservative)		    26 Oct   1951     --</p>
<p> Anthony Eden (Conservative)		  6 April 1955     58</p>
<p> Harold Macmillan (Conservative)	   10 Jan   1957     62</p>
<p> Alec Douglas-Home (Conservative)	  19 Oct   1963     60</p>
<p> Harold Wilson (Labour)			16 Oct   1964     48</p>
<p> Edward Heath (Conservative)		 19 June  1970     53</p>
<p> Wilson					     4 March 1974     --</p>
<p> James Callaghan (Labour)		     5 April 1976     64</p>
<p> Margaret Thatcher (Conservative)	   4 May   1979     53</p>
<p> John Major (Conservative)		   28 Nov   1990     47</p>
